---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Eligibility & Selection Criteria"
  description="Review the PGDBA eligibility requirements and shortlisting criteria for the personal interview."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-noir-900 via-noir-900 to-noir-950">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top,_rgba(86,142,174,0.65),_transparent_60%)]"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 text-center sm:py-20">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-noir-50 sm:text-5xl">
        Eligibility &amp; <span class="light-theme-highlight text-brand-400">Selection Criteria</span><span class="text-brand-500">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-noir-200">
        Check the academic qualifications required to apply and how candidates are shortlisted for the Personal Interview.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <aside class="info-callout mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 p-5 text-ink-800" role="note">
      <p class="font-semibold text-brand-800">For 2026 admissions</p>
      <p class="mt-1 leading-relaxed">
        The eligibility and selection criteria on this page are specific to 2026 admissions and may change for future admission cycles. Please check the official PGDBA admissions notification for authoritative, up-to-date requirements.
      </p>
    </aside>
    <div class="floating-card feature-card rounded-3xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
      <h2 class="section-heading font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 sm:text-3xl">
        Eligibility<span class="text-brand-600">.</span>
      </h2>
      <ul class="criteria-list reading-copy mt-6 space-y-5 text-ink-700">
        <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-600"></span>
          <span>
            A candidate must hold a graduate/postgraduate degree with 10 + 2 + 4 or 10 + 2 + 5 or 10 + 2 + 3 + 2, with at least <strong>60% marks or CGPA 6.5 on a 10-point scale</strong> in the Qualifying Degree (i.e., B.Tech./B.E./M.Sc./M.Com. or equivalent).
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-600"></span>
          <span>
            Candidates with 10 + 3 (Engineering diploma) + 3 (lateral entry into B.E./B.Tech.) with at least <strong>60% marks or CGPA 6.5 on a 10-point scale</strong> in the Qualifying Degree (i.e., B.Tech./B.E.), or with 10 + 2 + 4 (B.Sc.) with at least <strong>60% marks or CGPA 6.5 on a 10-point scale</strong> in the Qualifying Degree (i.e., B.Sc.), or with qualified CA/CS/ICWA/CMA with at least <strong>60% marks</strong> (Intermediate and Final examinations of the CA/CS/ICWA/CMA considered together) are also eligible.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-600"></span>
          <span>
            For SC/ST and Person with Benchmark Disability (PwBD) candidates, the qualifying marks for eligibility shall be <strong>55% or CGPA 6.0 on a 10-point scale</strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-600"></span>
          <span>
            The CGPA will not be converted into percentage marks even if the degree awarding Institute provides marks in CGPA system. Their admission will be based on the CGPA awarded in the transcript. If the CGPA is on a different scale than 10, the eligibility of a candidate will be based on the equivalence of the CGPA on a 10-point scale.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-600"></span>
          <span>
            Candidates, who are in the final year, are also eligible to apply provided they appear in the final examination and complete other academic requirements as specified above by <strong>Tuesday, 30th June 2026</strong>. For such cases, admission will be provisional subject to submission of final mark sheet by <strong>Monday, 30th November 2026</strong>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-600"></span>
          <span>
            <strong>In case of a foreign degree, the equivalence of the foreign degree needs to be certified by the Association of Indian Universities.</strong>
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="info-callout mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-ink-200 p-6 text-ink-800 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
      <h2 class="section-heading font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 sm:text-3xl">
        Shortlisting for Personal Interview<span class="text-brand-600">.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
        Candidates will be shortlisted for Personal Interview based on their score in the PGDBA Admission Test 2026. For woman and transgender candidates, an additional <strong>2 marks</strong> will be awarded as the <strong>gender diversity score</strong> for this shortlisting. These additional marks will <strong>not</strong> be considered for the final selection.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
